  "question": {
    "text": "If the probability that the random variable <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math> takes values <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math> is a constant, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math> is equal to",
